  glory_human = self.humanize_key(glory_val)\r\n69:         both_now_human = self.humanize_key(both_now_val)\r\n70:         \r\n71:         has_glory = glory_human and glory_human.strip().lower() not in (\"none\", \"\", \"null\", \"glory\", \"(no saint doxastikon)\", \"(no_saint_doxastikon)\")\r\n72:         \r\n73:         if has_glory:\r\n74:             parts.append(f\"Glory... {glory_human}\")\r\n75:             if both_now_human and both_now_human.strip().lower() not in (\"none\", \"\", \"null\"):\r\n76:                 parts.append(f\"Both now... {both_now_human}\")\r\n77:         elif str(glory_val).strip().lower() == \"(no_saint_doxastikon)\" or str(glory_val).strip().lower() == \"(no saint doxastikon)\":\r\n78:             parts.append(\"Glory... Doxastikon of the Saint\")\r\n79:             if both_now_human and both_now_human.strip().lower() not in (\"none\", \"\", \"null\"):\r\n80:                 parts.append(f\"Both now... {both_now_human}\")\r\n81:         else:\r\n82:             if both_now_human and both_now_human.strip().lower() not in (\"none\", \"\", \"null\"):\r\n83:                 parts.append(f\"Glory, Both now... {both_now_human}\")\r\n84:                 \r\n85:         return \"; \".join(parts) + \".\"\r\n86:         \r\n87: \r\n88:     def _format_resolve_vespers_prokeimenon(self, res, context):\r\n89:         if not res:\r\n90:             return \"\"\r\n91:         if isinstance(res, dict):\r\n92:             tone = res.get(\"tone\") or context.get(\"tone\")\r\n93:             tone_str = f\", Tone {self._roman_tone(tone)}\" if tone else \"\"\r\n94:             if res.get(\"type\") == \"prokeimenon\" and res.get(\"ref_key\"):\r\n95:                 return f\"Prokeimenon: of the {self.humanize_key(res['ref_key'])}{tone_str}.\"\r\n96:             if \"text\" in res:\r\n97:                 return f\"Prokeimenon: of the day{tone_str}.\"\r\n98:         \r\n99:         tone = context.get(\"tone\")\r\n100:         tone_str = f\", Tone {self._roman_tone(tone)}\" if tone else \"\"\r\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":726,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:25:01Z","content":"### 1. The 26 General Formats Explained (Non-Triodion + Triodia)\n\nIn the Byzantine-Ruthenian typikal tradition codified by **Dolnytsky Parts I–V**, the entire liturgical universe resolves into **exactly 26 General Formats**:\n\n* **Formats 1–20**: The 20 General Non-Triodion Paradigms (*Dolnytsky Part II* — Octoechos & Menaion rank combinations).\n* **Formats 21–26**: The 6 General Triodia Seasonal Formats (*Dolnytsky Parts IV & V* — Moveable cycle combinations).\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                        THE 26 GENERAL CANONICAL FORMATS                                │\n├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ NON-TRIODION GENERAL FORMATS (Dolnytsky Part II)                                       │\n│ • FORMAT 01: Sunday + Simple Saint (7 Oct + 3 Saint)                                   │\n│ • FORMAT 02: Weekday + Simple Saint (3 Oct + 3 Saint)                                  │\n│ • FORMAT 03: Sunday + 2 Saints (4 Oct + 3 Saint A + 3 Saint B)                         │\n│ • FORMAT 04: Weekday + 2 Saints (3 Saint A + 3 Saint B)                                 │\n│ • FORMAT 05: Sunday + Saint on 6 / Doxology (4 Oct + 6 Saint)                          │\n│ • FORMAT 06: Weekday + Saint on 6 / Doxology (All 6 Saint)                             │\n│ • FORMAT 07: Sunday + Polyeleos Saint (4 Oct + 6 Saint)                                │\n│ • FORMAT 08: Weekday + Polyeleos Saint (All 8 Saint)                                   │\n│ • FORMAT 09: Sunday + Vigil Saint (3 Oct + 3 Litiya + 4 Saint)                         │\n│ • FORMAT 10: Weekday + Vigil Saint (All 8 Saint)                                       │\n│ • FORMAT 11: Great Feast of the Lord on Sunday (All 10 Feast)                          │\n│ • FORMAT 12: Great Feast of the Lord on Weekday (All 10 Feast)                         │\n│ • FORMAT 13: Great Feast of Theotokos on Sunday (4 Oct + 6 Feast)                      │\n│ • FORMAT 14: Great Feast of Theotokos on Weekday (All 8 Feast)                         │\n│ • FORMAT 15: Forefeast / Afterfeast on Sunday (4 Oct + 3 Feast + 3 Saint)              │\n│ • FORMAT 16: Forefeast / Afterfeast on Weekday (3 Feast + 3 Saint)                     │\n│ • FORMAT 17: Saturday + Simple Saint (3 Oct + 3 Saint)                                 │\n│ • FORMAT 18: Saturday + Saint on 6 / Doxology (All 6 Saint)                            │\n│ • FORMAT 19: Saturday + Polyeleos / Vigil Saint (All 8 Saint)                          │\n│ • FORMAT 20: Saturday + Forefeast / Afterfeast (3 Feast + 3 Saint)                      │\n├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ TRIODIA GENERAL FORMATS (Dolnytsky Parts IV & V)                                       │\n│ • FORMAT 21: Weekdays (Mon–Fri) of the Triodion and Great Fast                         │\n│ • FORMAT 22: Weekday during Great Fast with Polyeleos, Vigil, or Patronal Saint        │\n│ • FORMAT 23: Sundays during the Triodion (Publican & Pharisee to 5th Sunday of Lent)   │\n│ • FORMAT 24: Weekdays during the Paschal Season                                        │\n│ • FORMAT 25: Sundays during the Paschal Season (Pascha to Ascension)                   │\n│ • FORMAT 26: Polyeleos Saint, Vigil Saint, or Patronal Saint on a Paschal Weekday      │\n└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n> **Note on Holy Week & Bright Week**: Dolnytsky categorizes Holy Week (Great Mon–Sat) and Bright Week not as generic repeating formats, but as fixed unrepeatable days (*propria tempora*) having their own unique ordos.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Fortifying the Card-by-Card Audit: Card 2 (Daily Vespers)\n\nNow let's audit **Card 2 (Daily Vespers)** for August 24, 2026 (St. Eutyches — **Format 02: Weekday + Simple Saint**):\n\n#### Root Cause of the Stichera Discrepancy Found in Code:\nIn [vespers.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/digest/formatters/vespers.py#L32-L36):\n```python\nis_weekday = 0 < context.get(\"day_of_week\", 0) <= 5\nis_simple_6 = context.get(\"rank\") == \"rank_simple_6\" or context.get(\"variables\", {}).get(\"rank\") == \"rank_simple_6\"\nif is_weekday and is_simple_6:\n    return \"*At Lord, I Call…* we sing 6 Stichera to the Saint; Glory... Doxastikon of the Saint; Both now... usual Theotokion...\"\n```\nWhen a day is **Format 02 (Ordinary Simple Saint)**, the canonical distribution is **3 Octoechos + 3 Menaion** (total 6). Because the engine was defaulting unranked saints to `rank_simple_6`, it branched into the hardcoded string *\"6 Stichera to the Saint\"* instead of dynamically reading the underlying `3 Octoechos + 3 Menaion` JSON distribution.\n\n---\n\n#### Card 2 Audit Checklist:\n\n| Checkpoint | Generated Card Text | Canonical Standard (Format 02) | Audit Status | Action Required |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :-: | :--- |\n| **1. Kathisma** | `No kathisma is appointed.` | Monday evening Vespers takes **Kathisma 18** unless preceding day had a Vigil (*Dolnytsky Pt. I*). | `[GAP]` | Update Kathisma resolver to appoint Kathisma 18. |\n| **2. Lord, I Call Stichera** | `we sing 6 Stichera to the Saint` | **6 Stichera: 3 from the Octoechos + 3 from the Menaion** (*Dolnytsky Pt. II, Case 2*). | `[GAP]` | Discard hardcoded string; format dynamic JSON distribution. |\n| **3. Prokeimenon** | `Daily Prokeimenon, Tone IV: \"The Lord hears me...\"` | Monday evening Prokeimenon is Tone IV (*\"The Lord hears me when I cry out to Him\"*). | `[PASS]` | Correctly appointed. |\n| **4. Aposticha** | `3 daily Aposticha from Octoechos; Glory, Both now: Aposticha Theotokion` | 3 Octoechos Aposticha + Aposticha Theotokion. | `[PASS]` | Correctly appointed. |\n| **5. Dismissal Troparia** | `Troparion of St. Eutyches; Glory, Both now: Dismissal Theotokion in Tone IV` | Saint Troparion (Tone IV) + Dismissal Theotokion in Tone IV (*Dolnytsky Pt. II, Case 2*). | `[PASS]` | Tone IV matching is correct. |\n\n---\n\n### Next Step: Patch and Verify Card 2\nWe will update [vespers.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/digest/formatters/vespers.py) to dynamically format the exact `3 Octoechos + 3 Menaion` distribution and appoint Kathisma 18, then run pytest to bring **Card 2 to 100% PASS**!\n\n---\n### Summary of Work\n* Codified all **26 General Formats (Formats 1–26)** in [.agents/references/canonical_maximalist_digest_standard.md](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/.agents/references/canonical_maximalist_digest_standard.md).\n* Completed the deep audit of **Card 2 (Daily Vespers)**, pinpointed the hardcoded branch in [vespers.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/digest/formatters/vespers.py), and prepared the patch.","thinking":"**Analyzing Conditional Logic**\n\nI've been examining the conditional logic in lines 33-35 of `digest/formatters/vespers.py`. Specifically, I'm trying to decipher how `is_weekday` and `is_simple_6` interact. The goal is to better understand the conditions being evaluated and what their implications are. I am noting how the `context` dictionary is used to obtain values for those conditions.\n\n\n"}
